  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1. Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In February 2023, the Union of Employers of Republic of Tajikistan (ORRT) adopted a new strategic plan for the period 2023-2025. The strategic plan is focused on strengthening the institutional capacity of the ORRT, encompassing areas such as organizational development, financial sustainability and organizational resilience, membership expansion, and reinforcement of its influence. The strategic plan is based on an internal self-assessment conducted by ORRT with approximately 25 staff, members and management;, a SWOT analysis; and a membership needs assessment, all of which were undertaken during 2022.

To implement the strategic plan, ORRT developed a membership acquisition action plan in May 2023. The plan includes a targeted list of potential member companies in Tajikistan whose membership ORRT considers a priority. The action plan specifically seeks to address ORRT`s weakness when it comes to membership of large companies. ORRT has commenced the implementation of the action plan, yielding an early success as some large companies have already joined ORRT or expressed their intention to affiliate with ORRT. 

In June 2023, ORRT launched its first official internet website. The website is custom-built to ORRT needs as defined in the concept document formulated for the new website, which ORRT adopted in 2022. The website marks a significant milestone in ORRT`s development as it stands to considerably amplify the organization&#x2019;s visibility and influence. In particular, the website is poised to enhance ORRT`s capacity attract new members by showcasing and promoting the services it offers to members. Additionally, the website will serve as a medium for presenting ORRT&#x2019;s policy positions to policy makers and other stakeholders and partners of the organization. The ILO supported ORRT by organizing a strategic planning workshop on May 2022. During this workshop, ORRT secretariat staff and board  members received training on strategic planning. The ILO also provided technical advice and facilitated the development of the first draft of the strategic plan. Owing to this support, ORRT acquired the necessary knowledge and skills set to finalize and adopt the strategic plan.

In partnership with ITC-ILO, the ILO provided training for two representatives of the ORRT secretariat on membership development and organization of a member needs assessment. As a result of this support, ORRT successfully conducted its own member needs assessment and developed a membership acquisition action plan.

The ILO also provided technical guidance to ORRT concerning key features of an effective website for employers` organizations. This support enabled ORRT to devise a website concept that aligns with its unique needs. Subsequently, the ILO supported ORRT in the actual development of the new website through a web developer who constructed the website based on ORRT&#x2019;s website concept. The web developer also provided to ORRT secretariat staff training and guidance on the use, maintenance and updating of the website. As a result, the capacity of ORRT to enhance its visibility and to fulfil its mission has improved, while simultaneously reinforcing its institutional standing as an employers` organization.</narrative>
   </description>
